1
00:06:21,176 --> 00:06:27,176
Two Generations. Two Wars. One Story

2
00:12:42,352 --> 00:12:48,352
Memorial Day is a action, drama, war film directed by Sam Fischer.

3
00:19:03,529 --> 00:19:09,529
Memorial Day, 1993.

4
00:25:24,705 --> 00:25:30,705
When 13-year-old Kyle Vogel discovers the World War II footlocker belonging
to his grandfather, Bud, everyone tells Kyle to put it back.

5
00:31:45,882 --> 00:31:51,882
Luckily, he ignores them.

6
00:38:07,058 --> 00:38:13,058
Although Bud has never talked about the war, he finds himself striking a deal with his grandson:
Kyle can pick any three souvenirs, and Bud will tell him the stories behind each one.

7
00:44:28,235 --> 00:44:34,235
Memorial Day not only takes us on a journey into Bud's complicated
wartime past, but also into Kyle's wartime future.

8
00:50:49,411 --> 00:50:55,411
As the two men share parallel experiences in combat, they come to realize
how that magical day on the porch shaped both of their lives.

9
00:57:10,588 --> 00:57:16,588
SSGT. Kyle Vogel, played by Jonathan Bennett.

10
01:03:31,764 --> 01:03:37,764
Bud Vogel, played by James Cromwell.

11
01:09:52,941 --> 01:09:58,941
Young Kyle Vogel, played by Jackson Bond.

12
01:16:14,117 --> 01:16:20,117
Lt. Kelly Tripp, played by Emily Fradenburgh.

13
01:22:35,294 --> 01:22:41,294
Brandt, played by Steven Luke.

14
01:28:56,470 --> 01:29:02,470
Memorial Day is a 2012 war film starring James Cromwell, Jonathan Bennett and
John Cromwell, directed by Sam Fischer and written by Marc Conklin.

15
01:35:17,647 --> 01:35:23,647
The film explores themes of war victim, military weapons,
warbird, insurgent, army national guard.

16
01:41:38,823 --> 01:41:44,823
The tone is emotional.
